The conversation focused on the description of coastal damages for a model report, particularly outlining categories such as inundation costs (loss of land and immobile capital), retreat costs (relocation and demolition expenses), protection costs (levy construction and maintenance), wetland loss (due to sea-level rise or protection), and extreme sea-level damages (capital loss and mortality). The model adopts methodologies from Diaz (2016) and incorporates critiques from Lincke and Hinkel (2021), ensuring a comprehensive approach to cost calculations associated with different scenarios of sea-level rise and adaptation strategies.
